WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:02.620
All right. I will now announce the prizewinner

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.500
for the best work in this round’s theme, yakisoba bread.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.570
The prizewinner for best work is
Koala of the New Tokyo Branch.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.470
We will award him the prize of 100,000 yen!

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.850
Well, it’s to be expected.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.000
After all, my Koala-chan is Pantasia’s best newcomer.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:26.440
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.310
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.610
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:39.240
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.840
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:01:00.120
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:08.090
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:15.930
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:23.680
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:31.150
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:40.530
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:49.290
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.550
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.510
is the light of only you.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.290
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:05.100
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:12.820
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.920
The green marvel!!

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.260
It’s the magician Kazuma!

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.350
Since Mizuno placed that bet
with so much confidence...

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:31.560
I expected him to be pretty skilled, but...

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.480
Mizuno is pretty confident about everything...

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.400
But, to think he defeated even Suwabara...!

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.160
Azuma!

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.700
The worst enemy you have in this newcomers’ battle may be Koala, not Suwabara...

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.000
No, I’m not really trying to scare you, Azuma...

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:53.380
I think Suwabara is a strong enemy too, but...

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.230
Kawachi!

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:58.070
Just because I’m listening quietly,
you’re just going on and on...

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.510
You heard...?

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:04.680
A fellow who can’t even judge the
loudness of his own voice...

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.330
won’t last on a battlefield!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.080
What’s he talking about?

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.430
Listen well.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:12.690
I’ll have you know that I didn’t
make any yakisoba bread.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.690
Wh... What?

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.320
What in the...?

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:26.200
Even if you don’t put it into words,
your back is speaking to me.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.660
Is that so?
Another win by default...

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.750
You couldn’t fight, could you?

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:32.670
I’m sorry...

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.420
Get this, Kawachi.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.710
Had I been able to make a bread myself,
beating you would have been nothing...

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:41.030
And I wouldn’t have lost against that Koala either.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.300
Remember that well.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:44.590
I can’t win against his intensity...

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.810
It’s not surprising that a more timid person would run...

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.180
I wonder if that’s really the case...

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:52.310
What was that?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.690
If you were watching the match, then...
I’m sure you realized it.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.480
That Koala is too strong!

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:04.300
Your yakisoba bread was...
for some reason, the best!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:04.970
Congratulations.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:07.570
I wonder if even you could’ve won...

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.500
His skill is that of a manager
of a famous first-class store.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.780
No. It may be above that.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.790
He’s not an opponent that a
newcomer can match up to.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:19.460
Damn it.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:21.440
No way...

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:23.670
Don’t worry.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:25.970
Ryuu-san.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.140
In that case,
I can just assassinate that Koala.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.970
And then the prize money will be mine!

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.910
Like I said... Something like that is no good, right?

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.190
I was joking.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:36.980
But...

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.020
That muscle... he’s on a different level than us.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.610
He’s definitely no ordinary guy.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.400
He seems to be quite an expert.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.700
I’d like to have a contest with him.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.930
Both of us being martial artists...

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.490
Oh. Hey! Ryuu-san!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.000
In honor of Koala’s highest grade, I now
present the prize of 100,000 yen!

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:53.700
Here you go!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.330
I am Ryuu Ryoumen.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.480
The successor of the ancient Chinese
assassination group Ryuuke Shinken.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:01.940
Now... I give you the usual challenge!

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:11.560
Wh... Who is he...?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:14.020
The prize is gone!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.040
100,000 yen
Prize for
best work

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.520
Ryuuke Shinken 100 Consecutive Flying Bird Kicks!

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.910
This fighting aura...

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.990
Just as I expected. He’s exceptional.

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:33.100
Just as I thought!

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.100
Koala is Mokoyama!!

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.250
Huh?

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:37.100
What?

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.000
A strange and dangerous intruder has been sighted!

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.110
Capture and hold him!

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:46.130
You... You say it’s Mokoyama?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.610
Yeah. There’s no mistake.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.010
I didn’t notice by his bread, but...

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:53.420
From his fighting aura, it’s now clear.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.100
Mokoyama and I worked at different
places in the past, but...

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.860
in order to acquire the powerful Solar Gauntlets,

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.130
we did similar training together.

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:10.140
There is no other baker capable of
emitting that kind of fighting aura.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.540
To... To be able to realize from something like that...

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.140
Honestly, what are these guys...?

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:16.870
Then...

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.500
Mokoyama-san was fired by St. Pierre...?

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.150
And there, Mizuno must have...

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:26.460
Yeah. St. Pierre’s owner isn’t the kind
of man who’d forgive a failure.

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:29.430
I guess it ended just as I feared...

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.970
Who the hell are you?

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:34.750
I’m going to tear off that mask no matter what.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.950
And I’m going to expose your true face.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:51.240
Another Koala from within the Koala?

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:54.350
No! That’s Mokoyama crying.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.790
I wonder what the circumstances are...

00:06:56.790 --> 00:07:00.850
In truth he must not have wanted
to fight in the newcomers’ battle.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.540
What are you doing?

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:03.960
Hurry up and subdue him!

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.130
Bring more men!

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:08.760
Damn it!

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.510
When did he get my prize...?

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:13.320
It’s a waste, but...
I’ll withdraw for now.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.070
Thi... This is the 4th floor.

00:07:30.070 --> 00:07:32.570
That was quite an interruption we had there, but...

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.570
In preparation for the schedule of the third round,

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:36.010
I’ll now announce the theme.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:40.620
The third round will be the same as the first
round, with the A group going first.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:42.420
We’ll have the match tomorrow.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.170
The B group goes the day after tomorrow.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:44.770
The theme is...

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:46.590
animal bread.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.800
What’s wrong?

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.340
Although I said “animal”...

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:56.030
any living being, from crabs to insects, will qualify.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:00.480
This time, artistic presentation will
be evaluated in addition to taste.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:04.100
We’re looking forward to unique designs
that will please women and children.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.600
That is all.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:09.360
Animal bread, huh?

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.050
It’s a surprisingly difficult bread, you know...

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.080
Right, Manager?

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.330
Hmm? Did you say something?

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.370
What’s up Manager? You’ve been
acting strange for a while.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.620
What happened?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:24.830
No, actually...

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.550
Animal bread is a surprisingly difficult bread, so...

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.840
Huh? That’s what I said.

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:35.580
It’s the bread which earned Mokoyama
the title, “God of sweetened buns.”

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.790
Amongst animal breads,
there’s a bread called “fish.”

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:44.020
Making it usually involves a technique
called “five-loop braiding.”

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:46.060
That helps make the delicate scales of the fish, but...

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.090
It’s quite difficult to make successfully.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.610
I know that.

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:55.700
It’s the thing listed under the most difficult
section of a textbook on baking, right?

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:58.370
But, if that’s all, it’s an easy win for even me.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:08:59.660
Is that so?

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:01.560
Then, how about a twenty-loop braid?

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:03.810
20 loops?!

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.920
It’s probably because Mokoyama’s disposition, but...

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.290
In contrast to his large frame...

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.840
he specializes in knitting.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.710
I wonder if Ken-chan will like this...?

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.470
Mokoyama probably has Japan’s
#1 bread braiding technique.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:21.100
He can use his twenty-loop braiding technique to form the scales of a dragon!

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.830
A dragon?!

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.990
Mokoyama probably has Japan’s
#1 bread braiding technique.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:58.490
He’s the man who can even make a dragon’s scales with his twenty-loop braiding technique!

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.470
Hmm...?

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.220
You shouldn’t be saying “Hmm...,” should you?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.770
He’s going to be your opponent, right?

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:06.600
Tha... That’s right...

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:07.230
On top of that...

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:11.460
This time Kuroyanagi said that artistic presentation will also be evaluated, right?

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.400
20-loop braiding means

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:16.490
that it’s four times the regular
five-loop braiding technique!

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:19.240
You can’t do such a thing, right?

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:20.950
Yeah, I can’t...

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:22.030
You moron!

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:25.160
Have you forgotten that Tsukino’s succession
fight is depending on this?

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.200
You won’t win if you don’t pull yourself together.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:30.710
I know that, but...

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:33.290
Whether or not you can do twenty-loop braiding

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.750
isn’t going to determine your victory or loss, right?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.720
That’s true I guess, but...

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.890
Oh no! It’s already this late.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:41.970
The shops will close.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.180
Tsukino... please come shopping with me again.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:45.960
O... Okay.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.600
You’ll fall if you run that fast!

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.600
Man...

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:54.210
He just doesn’t feel any pressure...
Does he have some way to win?

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:57.150
Well, his last match against this guy was a draw.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:10:59.450
I don’t think he’ll lose all that easily, but...

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:01.720
I wonder...

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:05.120
He trained at the same martial arts as me in the past...

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:08.960
The young Mokoyama was a
wonderful martial artist and...

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:13.250
a baker whose talent I envied.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:14.730
The Manager... envied him...?!

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.130
But...

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:21.800
His employment at St. Pierre turned him into a mere haughty, power hungry man.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.600
He’d leave the bread baking to his subordinates and...

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:25.720
he’d always be at beauty or nail art salons.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.250
Note: dojo is a hall used for martial arts training.
He stopped coming to the dojo as well.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:31.100
Earlier, I went up against him and

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.900
made Azuma fight him because...

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.150
What did you say?!

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:35.670
Try saying that again!

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.570
I’ll say it as many times as you want.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:42.910
An artisan of your level is no match for this boy.

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:46.450
Is Pantasia’s new bread, <i>Japan</i>, superior?

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.370
Or is St. Pierre’s new bread superior?

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:50.660
Let’s settle it... on TV.

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.710
Beautiful!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.020
I accept the challenge!

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.880
This is why you’re my Ken-chan!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.800
A man among men!

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.300
Of course...

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:04.390
advertising for the Southern Tokyo Branch
was the primary motive, but...

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.310
If Mokoyama could find his old self once again, then...

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.100
I had hoped a little for that as well...

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.310
Is that so...?

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:15.060
Mokoyama has lost everything...

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:17.570
He’s probably at the end of his tether...

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.860
There is no sign of the self-conceit which
he had the last time he faced Azuma.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.360
If he comes at him without worrying about anything...

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:25.320
Even Azuma definitely can’t win!

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:27.800
No... No way...

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:29.240
Guru Market

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:30.080
Azuma...
Guru Market

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.710
Guru Market

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:31.810
Let’s see... We got the spinach
and the powdered tea, right...?
Guru Market

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.170
Let’s see... We got the spinach
and the powdered tea, right...?

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.210
The mugwort and... And...
Note: mugwort is an aromatic culinary herb.

00:12:39.630 --> 00:12:43.340
But, we couldn’t find the most important thing...

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.590
There’s still more, Azuma-san?

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.350
I’m sorry, Tsukino.

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:50.020
We’ll have to go again tomorrow.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.560
I haven’t bought the most important thing.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.600
I don’t mind that, but...

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:58.610
Somehow everything seems to be green, right?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:12:59.770
Yeah!

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.590
Tomorrow, <i>Japan</i> #8 is going to be baked all in green.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:07.070
Baked all in green?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.230
Next Day

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:18.250
All right.

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.050
Starting now, the third round of the newcomers’ battle,

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:22.730
the quarterfinals for the A group will begin.

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:25.760
But, before that, the examiner...

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.010
That moron is late again.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.250
He really will be disqualified this time...

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:31.740
What should we do, Manager?

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.520
Well, that’s an inborn habit.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.520
It can’t be helped, can it?

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:39.690
It’s not here either...

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:41.750
What should we do, Azuma-san?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.780
If we don’t leave now, we won’t make it in time.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:46.280
But...

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:49.410
If we don’t have that,
I can’t make <i>Japan</i> #8.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.720
I can’t say anything to that.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.200
By the way, Azuma-san...

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.230
What in the world are we searching for...?

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.480
What is it?

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:01.480
A cheap candy store.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.510
Wai... Azuma-san...

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:08.180
Let’s see...

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.220
Umm... Azuma-san...
Let’s see...

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:10.140
Umm... Azuma-san...

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:12.470
What are you doing, Tsukino?

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:13.770
Come over here.

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:17.180
But... it’s the first time I’ve come to such a store...

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:22.730
But, Azuma-san! Don’t you have
to go find your important thing?

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:26.740
Yeah. The thing I was looking for is here.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:29.610
Oh my... And where’s Kazu-kun...?

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:31.180
Ah! Don’t tell me he’s run off.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:32.530
Mizuno!

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:35.200
I don’t see Tsukino-oneesan, either...

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.000
Hmm...?

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:40.250
Could it be that she’s given up on
being the successor and eloped?

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.260
Moron.

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:43.460
Oh, that’s right.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.510
Your name’s Kawachi or something, right?

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:46.200
What?

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.340
You’re also unexpectedly skillful, so...

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:50.680
Rather than working at the

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:53.850
Southern Tokyo Branch, which will have
no future once that woman has lost...

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.020
wouldn’t you rather work for us?

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.250
As a cashier.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:56.270
Check out
As a cashier.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:57.230
Check out

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.620
Thank you very much.
Check out

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:58.710
Thank you very much.

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:01.060
Hey! Why as a cashier?!

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.050
This little witch... talking too much...

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:05.050
See ya...

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.940
That flat-chested girl!

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.200
It’s now the quarterfinals!

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.070
Which means that examiner will be...

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:14.740
And... from the third round onward, the examiner will...

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:15.120
We made it!
And... from the third round onward, the examiner will...

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:15.740
We made it!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.790
Y... You’re late again...?

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.080
You dumbass!

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:27.960
How could you leave me here to be
insulted by that half-pint Mizuno?!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:29.970
Whatever...

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:31.930
I don’t even have the energy to be angry anymore.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:34.430
Even death won’t change Azuma’s tardiness.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.850
Well then, before starting the third round,

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:41.730
I wish to welcome the new examiner.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.850
Huh? Kuro-yan is being replaced?

00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.340
Who are you calling Kuro-yan?
Don’t get so familiar with me!

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.050
Don’t worry.
I’ll still be here of course.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.950
But from here on, even though you’re
newcomers, you’re the best eight.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:58.620
It would be difficult for just me to decide
on the outcome of the match.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:01.250
That’s why someone with greater capability and

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:04.560
judgment than me has been asked to come.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.460
To think that the proud Kuroyanagi accepts

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:10.090
someone as being more capable than him...

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.760
What kind of person can it be...
this examiner...

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:15.140
Don’t tell me! Meister...!

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:19.140
Wh... What?

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.790
And we have the sensei making his appearance!

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:23.190
He’s here.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.370
Wh-wh-wh-wh-wh... What the...?

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:47.840
What just happened?

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:50.360
Let me introduce you.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.590
The special examiner:
Dave Hashiguchi-sensei.

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.360
Aaah, so busy, so busy...

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:57.890
And... his assistant Haijima-san.

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:00.060
Dave Hashiguchi?

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.640
What...? It’s a name I’ve heard before.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.350
Dave Hashiguchi.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.690
He’s the author of the big hit manga Takitate Gohan.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.320
He’s released countless gourmet manga into the world.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:12.900
All of those were big hits.
A famous ex-manga artist.

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.400
Ex?

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:19.200
With money from royalties coming in, he started devouring gourmet delicacies greedily...

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:22.450
and began to get fat rapidly. Not only did he begin to stop doing his work,

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:25.390
he even forgot how to walk, and now his
movement solely relies on a bulldozer.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.710
Now, only the memory of how he was
busy all the time in the past remains...

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:32.590
And they say he can’t say anything other
than “Aaah, so busy, so busy.”

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:34.420
Aaah, so busy, so busy.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:36.930
Are... Are you sure about this?

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:40.220
Leaving other things aside,

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.430
there is no one who can compare to
him in his ability to taste things.

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:46.980
He’s called every year to the newcomers’ battle.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.630
Don’t tell me.
He breaks the wall every year?

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:52.900
So, since sensei has appeared as well...

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:54.630
we’ll start the third round.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:55.780
Begin!

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.390
All right!

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.280
Azuma.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.390
I won’t lose.

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.130
A... Amazing!

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.860
It’s like it’s Chinese martial arts.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.760
And compared to that... What the...?

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:21.140
He’s surrounded by grasses.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:23.810
All that green stuff...

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:26.580
Tsukino... what did Azuma take you to buy?

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:31.840
Well... He said he wanted to
bake the bread green... So...

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:33.860
A green bread, you say?

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:36.900
So, you mean that the dough inside is green?

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:41.030
No. He said that the outside would
also be green. Or something...

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:41.850
Huh?

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:44.660
You’re not a beginner either, so...

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:46.450
I think you know that...

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:51.460
you can’t possibly make a bread
that’s green on the outside.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:53.630
Once you bake bread, it becomes brown.

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:55.340
If it’s a steamed bread, then I understand, but...

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:58.360
Unless you use magic, you can’t
add color to a baked bread.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.880
I think so as well, but...

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:04.310
I wonder what Azuma is thinking...

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:07.870
If he loses in this round, you lose your bet as well.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:11.100
Oh yeah.

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.650
Would you like to eat these?

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:13.810
What?

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:16.980
We just bought it at a cheap candy store.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:21.070
Tsukino... You’re also saying quite the
carefree thing there, aren’t you...

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:23.320
It’s not the time to be eating sweets, is it?

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:24.140
Right, Manager?

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.300
Oh. You’re eating.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:30.390
What happened?

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.210
Tsukino...

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:35.610
Did Azuma buy starch syrup by any chance?

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:37.670
Manager!

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:38.990
How did you know...?

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:41.470
He definitely bought it.

00:19:41.470 --> 00:19:43.620
He was saying it’s the most important thing.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:45.390
Just as I thought.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:47.120
So, what happened?

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.480
Oh, the sticks coming off...

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:50.690
What the...?

00:19:50.690 --> 00:19:51.620
Kawachi!

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:54.270
I withdraw all previous remarks!

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.630
He may win!

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:58.190
Azuma will use magic.

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:00.130
Magic?

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.300
Amazing!

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:27.600
It’s a whole dragon!

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:31.310
That crystal-like shine is marmalade.

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:35.650
The luster of marmalade is making the
shine of the dragon more pronounced.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:37.980
This is...

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.320
This is like a fine art.

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:43.800
There’s really no way you can win
against this unless you use magic.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.610
That’s so true!

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:49.830
This time, presentation is also evaluated.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.830
I have no choice but to give this full marks.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:57.210
This is what Koala-chan’s true skill is...

00:20:57.210 --> 00:21:00.460
Give up on being the successor, okay, onee-san?

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:01.820
Not yet.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:04.340
Some more.

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:05.550
More.

00:21:06.090 --> 00:21:07.340
Some more.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:11.830
A blackout?

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:14.190
Don’t panic.

00:21:14.190 --> 00:21:16.900
In 20 seconds, the backup generators will start.

00:21:16.900 --> 00:21:18.110
It will have no effect on the ovens.

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:21.030
Azuma Kazuma.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:24.700
You seem to be taking your time baking it, but...

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.870
your defeat is now inevitable.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.950
But, Azuma Kazuma...

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:33.330
you can take all the time you want.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.920
Even if you lose, it’s just because
your opponent was too good.

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:39.060
You’re not trash.
I can affirm that.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:44.800
You’re rare without a doubt, and one of
the best newcomers in recent years.

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:47.560
I really enjoyed being with you.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.300
Thank you.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:51.890
And, goodbye, Azuma Kazuma.

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:53.600
Don’t be tardy any more.

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:55.080
It’s done!

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:11.870
Ma...

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:13.620
It’s magic!

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:14.850
The baked bread is...

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:26.150
It’s all green.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.150
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.150 --> 00:22:58.270
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.270 --> 00:23:00.270
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.570
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:04.490
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.490 --> 00:23:06.280
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.070
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:18.170
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:21.050
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:23.090
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:24.500
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.180 --> 00:23:29.300
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:31.140
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:36.690
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:57.500
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:08.570
That Azuma... He really made a green bread!

00:24:08.570 --> 00:24:09.970
Roar!

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:12.200
And Kuro-yan is flying!
And he’s breathing fire!

00:24:12.200 --> 00:24:14.200
He’s having a greater reaction than usual!

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:16.720
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,
The great decisive battle!!

00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:18.830
Koala’s dragon vs Kazuma’s turtle!

00:24:18.830 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.790
In Europe, braided breads are often
baked on celebratory occasions.

00:24:25.790 --> 00:24:27.050
In German, there’s a bread called Zopf.

00:24:27.050 --> 00:24:28.460
In the Lausanne region of Switzerland,

00:24:28.460 --> 00:24:31.720
it may have been the custom to give
braided breads instead of flowers.

00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:33.680
Yeah?!
